 p.sources.push({id:story,title:'Riverlight requests — original fiction',locator:'Authored world and quest scenario',excerpt:'This invented town has a quay, a walled garden and a signal tower. A parcel of labels waits at the quay for the gardener. Deliver it, then return with the gardener’s news to open a quay–archive shortcut. The garden keeper opens a separate archive path after a discussion of the evidence. Three trail tokens mark woodland, quay and archive exploration. After connecting the archive evidence, the traveller can repair a fictional three-wheel relay in the tower and choose the story’s next step. None of these mechanisms is a real water system or ecosystem intervention.'});
 p.world={title:'The Riverlight atlas',rooms:{
 quay:scene('The quiet quay','The evening ferry waits below a stone landing. A parcel sits beside the mooring ledger.','A parcel waiting for a name','The gardener has been waiting for these labels. A hand-written note asks the carrier to return with news; a nearby arch leads towards the archive, but its gate is shut.','Orin, the ferry keeper','“Everyone looks up at the dark tower. I keep looking at that parcel. If you pass the garden, I could use a hand.”',[story]),
 garden:scene('The walled garden','A glass conservatory catches the last light. There is work to finish before the evening signal.','The keeper’s field note',water?'In this fictional allocation, twelve units are available: four reserved for gardens and eight for homes. The garden’s share is one third of twelve. Protecting one share does not cancel the other.':'Grass uses sunlight to make its own food, so it is a producer. A rabbit eats grass; a fox can eat the rabbit. This is one food chain, not the whole web.','Lio, the garden keeper','“A label can point you in the right direction, but you still have to read the evidence. Help me decide what to write before we open the side path.”',[story,fact]),
 tower:scene('The waiting light','Three brass wheels stand beneath an unlit lantern. Beyond the arches, every path you walked meets the river.','A note beside the wheels','This signal is a fictional mechanism. Match each wheel’s open sides to the engraved route below it. The archive evidence has brought you here; the signal itself is a matter of tinkering.','Sable, the light keeper','“There is time. Turn a wheel, look at the route, and try again. Once the light returns, we can choose how tonight’s work begins.”',[story])},
 after:{workshop:'The mechanism sits steady now. Beyond it, the archive door stands open.',woods:'A small hollow marks where you found the trail token. The path continues towards the garden.',archive:'The evidence plates are connected. A trail of lamplight leads towards the tower stairs.',quay:'The parcel has reached its keeper. Orin has opened the archway: the archive is a short walk from the landing.',garden:'Lio pins the checked note beside the path and draws back the garden gate. The archive is within reach.',tower:'The lantern is lit. Warm gold runs over the brass wheels and out across the river.'},
 delivery:{title:'A label for every promise',parcelName:'Garden label parcel',offer:'“These labels belong in the walled garden. Please take them to Lio and bring back news.” You tuck the parcel into your journal pouch.',carrying:'“Still carrying the labels? Lio is in the walled garden. The path follows the water.”',delivered:'Lio unties the parcel. “At last! Tell Orin the labels arrived safely. We can read the field note while you are here.”',thanks:'“Good news travels on tired feet,” Orin says. “I have opened the archive arch for you. Thank you for coming back.”',sourceRefs:[story]},
 field:water?{title:'Protect the two shares',prompt:'Lio wants a label for the garden allocation. Which label matches the fictional ledger of twelve units?',options:['Gardens: four units, one third of the total','Gardens: eight units, two thirds of the total','Gardens: twelve units, the entire total'],solution:0,feedback:['Four out of twelve is one third. The remaining eight units stay reserved for homes.','Eight units belong to homes in this ledger. The garden share is four out of twelve.','Twelve is the combined total. The garden share is four; homes have eight reserved.'],hint:'The garden allocation is four out of twelve. Divide both numbers by four to see the fraction.',sourceRefs:[fact]}:{title:'A name beside the meadow',prompt:'Lio wants to label grass in the simplified food chain. Which explanation fits the evidence?',options:['A consumer: it gets its food by eating the rabbit','A producer: it makes its own food using sunlight','The entire food web: it includes every feeding relationship'],solution:1,feedback:['The rabbit eats the grass in this example. Grass makes its own food; it does not eat the rabbit.','Grass is a producer because it makes its own food using sunlight. This one route is part of a wider web.','A food web contains many feeding relationships. Grass is one producer, not the entire web.'],hint:'Look for how the grass gets its food. It uses sunlight rather than eating another organism.',sourceRefs:[fact]},
 relay:{title:'Light across the river',intro:'The signal waits on three brass elbows. Their engraved routes survived the years better than their moving parts. Bring the openings into line.',success:'The last connector settles into place. Light blooms above the wheels and reaches across the river. The neighbours are ready; the next choice is yours.',sourceRefs:[story]}};
 return validateAdventureContent(p);
